      "hardBoundaries": [
        "PrP-promoter reporter-positive nNOS-positive interneuron is one independent NeuroMorpho source object, not an average, archetype, molecular cluster, SCI entity, or morphology transferred from another record.",
        "The repository reports a 300 micrometre parasagittal source object, matching one paper protocol, but the paper does not expose this filename as an object crosswalk. The later 60 micrometre serial resectioning is a separate recovery stage and must not be collapsed into the initial slice-thickness field.",
